        "body": "Closed by MR !28, merged on 2026-10-08 as merge commit `05c76111f`. The plan's record is closed in\n`55c934d5c`.\n\n- `59bc44f45`: `extract_obj()` extracts what a sheath holds, beside the loop that extracts a\n  container's contents. Junking or selling a loaded sheath destroys its weapons with it, and the\n  leak after a rent save ends.\n- `2b8959cdd`: `Crash_save_pet()` writes a sheath's weapons as the pet's own objects beside the\n  sheath, as a house save does: no new table and no migration. A worn sheath's weapons are written\n  as inventory records, a carried sheath's at its own depth. The restored pet carries the weapons\n  and an empty sheath.\n- Review, `079e9bd6e`: a sheathed object knows its sheath (`sheathed_in`). `obj_to_sheath()` and\n  `obj_from_sheath()` set and clear the slot and the back-pointer together, so an object extracted\n  on its own (a deleted prototype, a timer that runs out) leaves its slot empty instead of a freed\n  address. `objs_from_sheath()`, which had no caller, is removed.\n- Review, `8a8f0fdd7`: `artifact_on_extract()` counts a sheathed object as placed, so a sheathed\n  artifact's destruction releases its ownership and is counted in the ledger.\n- Review, `da68e251a`: `delete_object()` hands a deleted sheath's weapons to its holder beside the\n  contents.\n- `docs/systems/SAVE_SYSTEMS_BREAKDOWN.md` has the pet rule, in the pets section.\n- Not changed here: the player sheath loader's debug trace (#33), `otransform`'s copy over a live\n  object (#34), and `Crash_extract_norents()`, which still does not walk a sheath's weapons.\n- No deploy: the fix reaches production with the next release.",
